{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Plugins","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"plugins.png"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A content bundle ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","isActive":true},{"text":") splits a game’s own world across types and packages. A plugin does something else: it packages a reusable ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"system","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — spellcasting, a wall clock, combat — so a second game can import it. The seven ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gnusto*"},{"type":"text","text":" libraries in this repo are all built this way, and so is the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"buy"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sell"},{"type":"text","text":" logic you would otherwise hand-copy into every shop game."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A plugin is ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"logic only","type":"text"}]},{"text":". It contributes the vocabulary its system needs and the rules that react to it, and owns no rooms, items, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" state; everything it touches is declared by the host game and handed to it as a parameter. A plugin that needs a room of its own is not a plugin.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"A-plugin-is-a-GamePlugin","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"A plugin is a `GamePlugin`"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["extension Intent {","    #verb(\"haggle\", [\"haggle\", \"over\", .directObject])","}","","struct CommercePlugin: GamePlugin {","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] {","        .haggle","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"actions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" all default to empty, so a plugin declares only what it needs. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"#verb","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" declarations (see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs"},{"text":") give the plugin ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}]},{"text":" its hosts the same typed constants — host rules key on ","type":"text"},{"code":".haggle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" exactly as the plugin’s verbs emit it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Note what ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"isn’t","type":"text"}]},{"text":" declared here. ","type":"text"},{"code":"buy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"sell","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are engine stub verbs (see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StubVerbs"},{"text":"), so the words are already in every game’s vocabulary; a commerce plugin only has to supply the behavior, which it does with the rules below. ","type":"text"},{"code":"haggle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is genuinely the plugin’s own, so it needs the ","type":"text"},{"code":"#verb","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoMeleeCombat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" splits the same way: the ","type":"text"},{"code":"attack","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" family is promoted, ","type":"text"},{"code":"stab","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"strike","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are added.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" splice the same way (","type":"text"},{"code":"var timers: [TimedEvent] { actors.timers }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and parameterized timer ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"factories","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — methods returning a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TimedEvent","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the host’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block — are how a plugin animates the host’s actors on the end-of-turn clock. A bare timer name the host or another bundle also declares is namespaced into the declaring bundle’s namespace at bootstrap, so prefixes are a courtesy rather than a requirement (","type":"text"},{"code":"\"actors.roam\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") — but an unambiguous name keeps its bare schedule key, which is also its save-file key.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-host-splices-verbs-and-rules","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The host splices verbs and rules"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host stores the plugin as a plain property and splices its vocabulary into its own "},{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block. A plain plugin property is neither a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", nor "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"type":"text","text":", so the bootstrap’s reflection walk ignores it — it never becomes an entity and never collides."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".price"},{"type":"text","text":" below is a "},{"code":"TraitKey<Int>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" declared once ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"extension TraitKey<Int> { static let price = Self(\"price\") }"},{"type":"text","text":") — see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct LampShop: Game {","    let commerce = CommercePlugin()","    @Global var purse = Purse(coins: 10)          \/\/ the HOST owns the wallet","    let lantern = Item { name(\"brass lantern\"); trait(.price, 5) }","","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] { commerce.verbs }    \/\/ splice the vocabulary","    \/\/ rules below","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Parameterized rules over host entities","type":"heading","anchor":"Parameterized-rules-over-host-entities"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin’s rules need the host’s own lantern and purse — things it can’t know about in advance. So rules that touch host state are exposed as ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"parameterized methods","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" returning ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which the host calls with its own declarations. The wallet is handed in as closures that read and adjust the host’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"text":"; they run under the live turn, so they see and mutate state exactly as an inline rule would.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["extension CommercePlugin {","    @RuleBuilder","    func purchase(","        of item: Item,","        balance: @escaping @Sendable () -> Int,","        charge:  @escaping @Sendable (Int) -> Void","    ) -> Rules {","        item.before(.buy) {","            let price = item[.price] ?? 0","            guard balance() >= price else {","                try refuse(\"You can't afford the \\(item.name); it costs \\(price) coins.\")","            }","            charge(price)","            try reply(\"You buy the \\(item.name) for \\(price) coins. You have \\(balance()) left.\")","        }","    }","}","","\/\/ in the host:","var rules: Rules {","    commerce.purchase(of: lantern,","                      balance: { purse.coins },","                      charge:  { purse.coins -= $0 })","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The protocol’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" requirement is for self-contained, world-scoped rules that need nothing from the host; anything host-specific goes through a factory method like this.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"A plugin can contribute only vocabulary","type":"heading","anchor":"A-plugin-can-contribute-only-vocabulary"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The rules are optional. A plugin can teach the parser a word and leave the behavior to the host, which handles the shared intent in its own ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["extension Intent {","    #verb(\"appraise\", [\"appraise\", .directObject])","}","","struct Appraiser: GamePlugin {","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] {","        .appraise","    }","}","","\/\/ in the host:","var rules: Rules {","    gem.before(.appraise) {","        try reply(\"The \\(gem.name) is worth \\(gem[.price] ?? 0) coins.\")","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"The one thing the host doesn’t splice","type":"heading","anchor":"The-one-thing-the-host-doesnt-splice"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin\/statusFields","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" adds ","type":"text"},{"code":"name=value","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pairs to the play-test status footer, and it is the single member the host gets by ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"storing"}]},{"text":" the plugin rather than by splicing it into a block of its own:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct Barometer: GamePlugin {","    var statusFields: [(String, String)] { [(\"glass\", \"falling\")] }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything else here changes what the game does, so the host opts in by hand. A status field annotates a transcript the host already asked for and changes nothing about the world — and there is no "},{"code":"Game","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block to splice it into — so the bootstrap reads it off the host’s stored properties, the same walk that catches an unlisted bundle. A plugin the host stores is found; one constructed inline inside a computed property is not.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The field is read inside a live turn frame that is then discarded, so it must be read-only — and it is sampled at the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"close"}]},{"type":"text","text":" of the turn rather than after the turn’s counter advanced, so a field derived from "},{"code":"moves","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" names the turn it is printed under. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles#A-bundle-can-add-a-field-to-the-status-footer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the full contract, sampling point included, which is identical for both protocols."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Content-bearing-plugins-own-their-region","text":"Content-bearing plugins own their region"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A logic-only "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" declares no world of its own — it operates entirely over entities the host passes it. A plugin that needs to ship its "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"own","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" rooms, items, and "},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" state is a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instead: a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" carries "},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the bootstrap discovers its entities by reflection, "},{"overridingTitle":"namespacing","type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles#EntityIDs-are-namespaced-by-the-bundle","isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"namespacing","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" them under the bundle so a reusable plugin can’t collide with the host. List it in the game’s "},{"code":"content","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The two roles compose in one type. A single struct can conform to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (for its auto-namespaced region and self-contained rules) "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" expose host-facing rule factories exactly like a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — factories are just methods returning "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", so any type can offer them:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["extension Intent {","    #verb(\"donate\", [\"donate\", .directObject])","}","","struct ShrineContent: GameContent {","    let shrine = Location { name(\"Stone Shrine\"); description(\"…\") }   \/\/ its own room","    @Global var visits = 0                                             \/\/ its own state","","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] { .donate }","    var rules: Rules { shrine.onEnter { visits += 1; try reply(\"…\") } }  \/\/ self-contained","","    \/\/ Host-facing factory over a host item + host global — the GamePlugin pattern.","    func offering(of item: Item,","                  merit: @escaping @Sendable () -> Int,","                  credit: @escaping @Sendable (Int) -> Void) -> Rules {","        item.before(.donate) { credit(item[.value] ?? 0)","            try reply(\"Your merit rises to \\(merit()).\") }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host lists it in "},{"code":"content","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (registering the namespaced region) "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" splices the factory into its own "},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", wiring it to host declarations:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct PilgrimGame: Game {","    let shrineKit = ShrineContent()","    @Global var merit = 0","    let coin = Item { name(\"brass coin\"); trait(.value, 7) }","","    var content: GameContents { shrineKit }","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] { shrineKit.verbs }","    var rules: Rules {","        shrineKit.offering(of: coin, merit: { merit }, credit: { merit += $0 })","    }","    \/\/ map: place coin in shrineKit.shrine, wire plaza ↔ shrineKit.shrine, …","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"References stay token-based across the boundary, so a host item can sit in a plugin room and a plugin rule can hook a host entity regardless of the namespace."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"The-first-party-plugins","text":"The first-party plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Seven shipped library products exercise both plugin shapes for real — each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"imports only "},{"code":"Gnusto","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the Zork 1 executable target is the worked"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"example that wires the first four:"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Product","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Shape","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Owns","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The host passes","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoDangerousDark","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one dark-turn counter, the grue daemon","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" + grace period at init; ","type":"text"},{"code":"suspended","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to make the dark harmless for a stretch (never ","type":"text"},{"code":"stopDaemon(\"grue\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which freezes the count)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoScoring","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"award-once registers","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"the award table to ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(awards:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", treasures + the trophy case to ","type":"text"},{"code":"treasures(_:into:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoActors","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GamePlugin","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"nothing — position ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"is"}]},{"text":" the actor’s placement","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"actors, room sets, candidates to ","type":"text"},{"code":"roams","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"steals","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"reaction","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoMeleeCombat","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"the combat ledger (health\/stun\/engagement by key)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"villains, weapons, prose to ","type":"text"},{"code":"villain","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"aggression","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and each villain’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"strikesFirst","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" odds of picking a fight nobody offered him","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoSpellcasting","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the spell memory and the energy pool"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"spells + their "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SpellCost"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"code":"spell(_:called:cost:effect:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the system’s own refusals and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"spells","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" report","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoClock","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the clock’s offset and pause state"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"start time, minutes per turn, alarms to "},{"code":"at(_:named:perform:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", timetables to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"schedule(_:named:_:)"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GnustoConversation","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"the facts the player has worked out, and which answers each actor has already given","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"actors + topic rows to "},{"code":"topics(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (with "},{"code":"again:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lines for the answers that should land once), opening lines to ","type":"text"},{"code":"greeting(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", evidence to ","type":"text"},{"code":"shows(_:to:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Three spellings are shared across the set, so a label learned in one library holds in the next. A daemon or alarm a library declares takes its timer name as "},{"code":"named:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"roams(thief, named: \"thief.roams\", …)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"at(time, named: \"clock.blast\")"},{"type":"text","text":" — and the engine’s own "},{"code":"daemon(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fuse(_:after:)"},{"type":"text","text":" take theirs unlabeled. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"() -> Bool"},{"text":" gate is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"when:"},{"type":"text","text":", in a library as in a conditional exit or a topic row. And every library that prints a line of its own takes a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Text"},{"text":" at init — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MeleeCombat.Text"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Conversation.Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Spellcasting.Text"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DangerousDark.Text"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Clock.Text"},{"type":"text","text":" — with the stock wording as the default, so a game re-voices the lines it cares about and leaves the rest."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The split follows one rule: a system that needs its own saved state is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"},{"type":"text","text":" bundle (its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Global"},{"type":"text","text":"s namespace automatically and travel in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"saves); a stateless toolkit is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GamePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":". Plugin prose arrives as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"init and factory parameters"}]},{"type":"text","text":" with sensible defaults — "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fixed struct, so a plugin can’t add lines to it retroactively; what it can"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"do is take its lines from the host, which also keeps every player-visible"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"string in the game’s own voice.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Worked-examples","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Worked examples"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/Lighthouse\/"},{"text":" — a small host that splices just two: ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoScoring","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"visit"},{"text":" award and a one-off ","type":"text"},{"code":"awardOnce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", both declared in its award table so the bootstrap can check "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxScore"},{"type":"text","text":") and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoActors"},{"type":"text","text":" (a roaming keeper). The smallest of these examples."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/Zork1\/Zork1.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" — the host that wires "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoActors"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoDangerousDark"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoMeleeCombat"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoScoring"},{"type":"text","text":" over entities declared in its own content bundles."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/Gramarye\/Gramarye.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" — a small original game built entirely around "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoSpellcasting"},{"type":"text","text":", with one puzzle per casting paradigm."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/Fulminate\/Fulminate.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" — the mystery demo, built around "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoClock"},{"type":"text","text":": an evening on a wall clock with three alarms bracketing it. Its story and mechanics contract live in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"docs\/games\/fulminate.md"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/KindlyDeep\/"},{"type":"text","text":" — a survival-and-companion host: "},{"code":"GnustoActors.follows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a mule who trails you, is parked by a crawl he cannot fit through, and rejoins through a door, plus ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoScoring.awardOnce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on each of its five beats.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Tests\/GnustoTests\/Support\/CommerceGame.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the logic-only commerce plugin (","type":"text"},{"code":"buy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"sell","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" verbs, ","type":"text"},{"code":"purchase","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"sale","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" factories, ","type":"text"},{"code":"LampShop","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" host); ","type":"text"},{"code":"PluginTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" drives a buy\/sell turn end to end.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Tests\/GnustoTests\/Support\/ShrineContent.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the content-bearing ","type":"text"},{"code":"ShrineContent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin (owns a namespaced shrine region ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" exposes an ","type":"text"},{"code":"offering","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" factory) with its ","type":"text"},{"code":"PilgrimGame","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" host; ","type":"text"},{"code":"ContentPluginTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" drives a donate turn across the namespace boundary and checks the namespacing.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"Plugins","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/plugins"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Package a reusable game system as an importable unit of verbs and rules."}],"seeAlsoSection